# Median sum of squares — four times the sum of squared medians equals three times the sum of squared sides (source: classical; Altshiller-Court)
A B C = triangle
Ma = midpoint(B, C)
Mb = midpoint(C, A)
Mc = midpoint(A, B)
prove 4 * dist(A, Ma) ^ 2 + 4 * dist(B, Mb) ^ 2 + 4 * dist(C, Mc) ^ 2 = 3 * dist(A, B) ^ 2 + 3 * dist(B, C) ^ 2 + 3 * dist(C, A) ^ 2
